      "id": "co2",
      "title": "Atmospheric CO2",
      "description": "Carbon dioxide moving through the atmosphere from NASA's DYAMOND simulation with the GEOS model, over the whole planet. The timeline moves every region in 12 steps of six hours. NASA shows it as a turning globe, so no frame shows the whole planet at one moment: each side comes from its own stretch of the animation (Asia and Australia 14-17 January 2020, India 24-27 January, Africa and the Middle East 3-5 February, Europe and West Africa 12-15 February, the Americas and the Atlantic 23-25 February, western North America and the eastern Pacific 1-3 March); the Americas side decides alone around the Amazon, and elsewhere, where two sides meet, their dates are blended. It is the global context, not a measured effect of the Amazon. More CO2 makes the breathing pulse faster and heavier.",
      "source": {
        "title": "DYAMOND Global Carbon Dioxide (NASA SVS 5196)",
